            'note' => 'To sign: author hashes message and encrypts hash with their PRIVATE key; anyone with sender\'s PUBLIC key decrypts signature and compares against message hash to verify authenticity (Non-Repudiation). Encryption uses recipient\'s PUBLIC key; decryption uses recipient\'s PRIVATE key.',
        ],
        [
            'text' => 'Explain the Diffie-Hellman Key Exchange protocol. How do Alice and Bob establish a shared secret over an insecure channel without transmitting the secret itself?',
            'category' => 'technical',
            'duration_seconds' => 180,
            'note' => 'Agree on public prime p and base g. Alice picks secret a, sends $A = g^a \\pmod p$; Bob picks secret b, sends $B = g^b \\pmod p$. Alice computes $s = B^a \\pmod p = g^{ab} \\pmod p$; Bob computes $s = A^b \\pmod p = g^{ab} \\pmod p$. Eavesdropper cannot compute secret due to Discrete Logarithm Problem hardness.',
